  {
   "title": "How axions decay",
   "text": [
    "An axion-like particle couples to photons and electrons. For eV–GeV masses it is long-lived, yet a tiny fraction decays inside every galaxy."
   ],
   "math": [
    "\\mathcal L\\supset-\\tfrac14\\,g_{a\\gamma\\gamma}\\,a\\,F_{\\mu\\nu}\\tilde F^{\\mu\\nu}-i\\,g_{aee}\\,a\\,\\bar e\\gamma_5 e",
    "\\Gamma_{a\\to\\gamma\\gamma}=\\frac{g_{a\\gamma\\gamma}^2\\,m_a^3}{64\\pi},\\qquad\\Gamma_{a\\to e^+e^-}=\\frac{g_{aee}^2\\,m_a}{8\\pi}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{4m_e^2}{m_a^2}}"
   ]
  },
